      {
        "id": 3370252685,
        "node_id": "PR_kwDOLDdqOc7I4fmN",
        "number": 66,
        "state": "closed",
        "title": "fix: normalize queryMany response for single-query input",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #38.\n\nWhen `queryMany` is called with a single query in the array (e.g. `index.queryMany([{ vector: [...], topK: 6 }])`), the Upstash API returns a flat `QueryResult[]` instead of the expected nested `QueryResult[][]`. This causes the return type to violate the declared TypeScript signature, leading to runtime errors when callers index into `result[0]` expecting an inner array.\n\nThis PR overrides `exec()` in `QueryManyCommand` to detect and normalize the flat response by wrapping it in an outer array when a single query was provided. The fix:\n\n- Tracks the query count from the constructor payload\n- After receiving the API response, checks if the first element is a plain result object (not an array)\n- If so, wraps the result to maintain the `QueryResult<TMetadata>[][]` contract\n\nThis ensures `queryMany` always returns a consistent nested array regardless of how many queries are provided.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- Added test: `\"should return nested array when single query is provided\"` — validates `QueryManyCommand` directly with a single query\n- Added test: `\"should return nested array with single query via Index client\"` — validates the same behavior through the `Index.queryMany` API\n- Both tests assert `Array.isArray(res[0])` to confirm nested structure\n- Existing multi-query tests remain unchanged and continue to pass\n\n---\n\n> **AI Disclosure:** This PR was authored by Claude (Opus 4.6), an AI assistant made by Anthropic, operating transparently under human direction. See https://maxcalkin.com/ai for details.",
        "html_url": "https://github.com/upstash/vector-js/pull/66",
        "created_at": "2026-03-08T17:49:29Z",
        "updated_at": "2026-03-09T11:52:57Z",
        "closed_at": "2026-03-09T11:52:57Z",
        "merged_at": "2026-03-09T11:52:56Z",
        "merge_commit_sha": "02d3a2a2fb75284a559f9263eb468fbab95b9fc8",
